+### Repeatable bot scenarios
+
+`tools/run-bot-scenarios.sh` compiles the real game simulation for a standalone Java 17+ runtime.
+It runs all 26 maps in their recommended modes plus controls for passive bots, weapon and movement
+modifiers. `--long` expands to two passes across arena modes; `--maps=23,24,25 --long --players=100`
+exercises both Battlefield planners at the maximum population. `--seconds=90`, `--seed=...`,
+`--output=...` and `--strict` customize duration, deterministic seeds, report directory and warning
+handling. The runner writes checkpointed JSON/CSV with per-bot and aggregate movement, intentional
+holds, blocked intent, idle time, continuous spinning, repeated failed goals, recovery and timing.
+`Match.enableBotDiagnostics()` is opt-in; normal matches neither allocate nor sample this telemetry.
+Intent is captured before collision and sampled afterward. Countdown, deaths, respawn teleports,
+Range targets, cover, objective holds and investigation pauses are classified separately. Published
+thresholds flag individuals as well as team averages. Timing covers desktop JVM `Match.update`
+using Java voxel fallbacks, not Android rendering, audio, JNI or measured device frame rate.
 
